# Every *.py / *.sh tracked in this repository, and why it may exist (docs/93-devtools.md "What is
# not C++"). `mcppls-devtools check scripts` fails on a tracked script not listed here, on an entry
# whose script is gone, and on an entry without a reason. Format: `<path>`, a tab, the reason;
# blank lines and lines starting with '#' are comments.

docs/specs/tools/validate.py	JSON Schema 2020-12 validation, and no C++ library in the mcpp index supports it yet; ported when one does, or when the schemas can say the same in draft-07.
.github/scripts/install-mcpp.sh	CI bootstrap: installs mcpp itself, before any mcpp-built program can run.
.github/scripts/wait-engine-candidate.py	CI input admission: queries GitHub run/job/artifact metadata before any mcpp-built payload assembler runs; waits for all five immutable engine parts and their exact run/head while independent server builds proceed.
.github/scripts/test_wait_engine_candidate.py	CI input admission controls: incomplete parts, failed jobs, changed run/head, missing bundle identity, stale or malformed artifacts, and retry attempts cannot bypass the payload gate.
.github/scripts/timing_evidence.py	CI timing diagnostics: captures bounded per-round engine reports and cache log excerpts around the native conformance executable; preserves its exit status and keeps collection outside measured latency.
editors/zed/tests/smoke.sh	The real-Zed smoke (plan 0.0.8 part 2 Z-2, Z-3): drives a GUI editor binary under xvfb, starts and stops it, and inspects its process tree; that is shell work, and no mcpp-built program can stand in for Zed.
editors/zed/tests/lsp_frames.py	The smoke's helper that reads the LSP frames a wrapper recorded between Zed and mcppls; kept beside smoke.sh, which needs it only in the same CI job.
editors/zed/tests/payload_processes.py	The Linux GUI smoke's process observer: reads /proc and the installed payload manifest to distinguish the server and its engine even when both run through the same loader; used only beside smoke.sh in that CI job.
editors/zed/tests/test_payload_processes.py	CI controls for the GUI smoke's observer: real parent/child processes sharing an executable, unrelated images, native executables and a dead engine, before either real Zed mode runs.
.github/scripts/stability_evidence.py	CI stability diagnostics: retains bounded text logs, CDB excerpts and measurements for each native conformance round, preserves its verdict, and cleans its owned scratch after collection.
.github/scripts/publish-jetbrains.py	Release distribution: verifies the immutable CLion archive digest and plugin descriptor, then submits one Marketplace upload after the product is built; this CI-only publisher uses the host's HTTP and ZIP libraries.
.github/scripts/archive-tests.py	CI test transport: verifies and streams mcpp-produced test archive parts into one container per package, reclaiming only verified executable bytes on the cross-build host before native tests run.
.github/scripts/test_archive_tests.py	CI test transport controls: exercises the archive merger with discovered test names, PAX paths, changed common payloads and corrupt archives before any real executable is reclaimed.
